    "fileId": 51672,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Sclerosing adenosis mimics invasive carcinoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Ductal carcinoma in&nbsp;situ involving sclerosing adenosis mimics invasive carcinoma. The affected terminal duct lobular unit consists of tubules with a lobulocentric arrangement, similar to the adjacent sclerosing adenosis. Such a growth pattern should prompt further evaluation with immunohistochemical markers.",
    "source": "Edi Brogi",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/84/13/51672.jpg",
